  {"i":152,"t":["actions"],"n":"Basic general verb 'to live'; 'people' is only a loose association, so actions alone."},
  {"i":162,"t":["function"],"n":"っていう (〜っていう人, 〜っていう意味) is taught as a quotative and naming grammar pattern, not in a communication unit."},
  {"i":181,"t":["function","numbers"],"n":"まず is mainly a sequencing and discourse adverb (まず、次に…), so function comes first; the 'first' order sense keeps numbers."},
  {"i":186,"t":["function"],"n":"〜たばかり is a grammar pattern covered by function; a separate time sense entry is unnecessary."},
  {"i":198,"t":["qualities"],"n":"Describes things or situations as funny, strange or wrong; it is an evaluative adjective, not an emotion word."},
  {"i":210,"t":["function"],"n":"〜のせい is taught as a grammar pattern of cause and blame; 'thinking' is loose."},
  {"i":223,"t":["time","position"],"n":"Suffix ちゅう is mostly 'during / in the middle of' (会議中, 今週中), so time comes first; 'within/among' (世界中) keeps position."},
  {"i":238,"t":["food"],"n":"Tableware is taught in the food unit; home adds nothing."},
  {"i":268,"t":["money","shopping","function"],"n":"いくらですか is first met when asking prices in the money and shopping units; its question-word role comes after that."}
